# TWRP runs as the recovery domain and needs far broader access than stock
# recovery: rootfs writes, twrp.* properties, device-mapper ioctls for logical
# partitions, and mounting vendor_dlkm to load touch modules. Enumerating every
# allow rule would take many build/flash cycles and the recovery environment is
# root-by-design anyway (reaching it already requires an unlocked bootloader).
permissive recovery;
